[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3843318955","pull_request_review_id":5007634338,"id":3843318955,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7lFGSr","diff_hunk":"@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@\n #include \"core/math/vector3.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/local_vector.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/pooled_list.h\"\n+#include \"core/variant/variant.h\"","path":"core/math/bvh_tree.h","commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","original_commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I don't think this include is necessary. It gets included transitively but I don't think anything in bvh_tree requires it explicity or am I missing something?","created_at":"2026-08-24T12:11:57Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T12:11:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3843318955","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3843318955"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3843318955"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3843318955/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":46,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3848246921","pull_request_review_id":5013475684,"id":3848246921,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7lX5aJ","diff_hunk":"@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@\n #include \"core/math/vector3.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/local_vector.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/pooled_list.h\"\n+#include \"core/variant/variant.h\"","path":"core/math/bvh_tree.h","commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","original_commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Good find, as variant.h is big and complex. Some additional `#include` is certainly needed in order to compile the `Pair` template added by this PR.\r\n\r\nTooling will mark the header as unnecessary because it doesn't look into `#include \"bvh_cull.inc\"` further down in the `bvh_tree.h` file.\r\n\r\nIn addition to the new use of `Pair`, the engine will not compile if you enable the BVH_VERBOSE macro shown below (I suspect no one has uncommented these macros for many years).\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n// never do these checks in release\r\n#ifdef DEV_ENABLED\r\n//#define BVH_VERBOSE\r\n//#define BVH_VERBOSE_TREE\r\n//#define BVH_VERBOSE_PAIRING\r\n//#define BVH_VERBOSE_MOVES\r\n\r\n//#define BVH_VERBOSE_FRAME\r\n//#define BVH_CHECKS\r\n//#define BVH_INTEGRITY_CHECKS\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo bringing in `variant.h` solved both problems simply, but `variant.h` is big, with more stuff than I need. So I have pushed a commit that includes less total code. Instead of `variant.h`, it brings in `pair.h`, and it brings in `print_string.h` only if DEV_ENABLED and BVH_VERBOSE are true. \r\n\r\nI also rearranged the #defines to try to ensure there aren't too many macros defined before `#include` files.","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:19:23Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T00:52:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3848246921","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3848246921"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3848246921"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3848246921/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":46,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3843318955,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3849547225","pull_request_review_id":5014928697,"id":3849547225,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7lc23Z","diff_hunk":"@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@\n #include \"core/math/vector3.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/local_vector.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/pooled_list.h\"\n+#include \"core/variant/variant.h\"","path":"core/math/bvh_tree.h","commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","original_commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> (I suspect no one has uncommented these macros for many years)\r\n\r\nYes, and I likely only made heavy use of them in 3.x as that was the master / development version.\r\n\r\nI aimed to keep BVH in 3.x in sync (aside from small renames that were done in 4.x like `is_empty()` etc changing on containers).\r\n\r\nWith the use of thread pools that will likely have to change a little, as they aren't present / available in the same way in 3.x if I remember right. However if we can keep them as \"swappable\" as possible that will be advantageous, so if we fix a bug in one we can immediately fix it in the other and keep them up to date.","created_at":"2026-08-25T04:23:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T04:23:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3849547225","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3849547225"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3849547225"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3849547225/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":46,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3843318955,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3851883544","pull_request_review_id":5017633327,"id":3851883544,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7llxQY","diff_hunk":"@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@\n #include \"core/math/vector3.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/local_vector.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/pooled_list.h\"\n+#include \"core/variant/variant.h\"","path":"core/math/bvh_tree.h","commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","original_commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It would be nice to keep them in sync. \r\n\r\nRather than a template parameter (or in addition), I could use defines for multithreading? That would keep them swappable.","created_at":"2026-08-25T10:06:52Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:06:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3851883544","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3851883544"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3851883544"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3851883544/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":46,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3843318955,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3851935318","pull_request_review_id":5017691051,"id":3851935318,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7ll95W","diff_hunk":"@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@\n #include \"core/math/vector3.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/local_vector.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/pooled_list.h\"\n+#include \"core/variant/variant.h\"","path":"core/math/bvh_tree.h","commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","original_commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yeah, difficult to know the best way. If we literally only use the BVH for `GodotPhysics`, then a single define would do, but I'm not sure that is a good idea in case we use it for something else in 4.x that doesn't need threads.\r\n\r\nSo probably we would need a define _AND_ a template param to keep them in sync, which is a little ugly, but maybe it's still worth it.\r\n\r\nThe other thing that might be worth doing is isolating the threading code into a separate `.inc` file, just in terms of separation of concerns. What do you think? :thinking: ","created_at":"2026-08-25T10:12:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:12:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3851935318","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3851935318"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3851935318"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3851935318/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":46,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3843318955,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3852270781","pull_request_review_id":5018069437,"id":3852270781,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7lnPy9","diff_hunk":"@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@\n #include \"core/math/vector3.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/local_vector.h\"\n #include \"core/templates/pooled_list.h\"\n+#include \"core/variant/variant.h\"","path":"core/math/bvh_tree.h","commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","original_commit_id":"6883e965000f78873c02dae3a51497c9858c7fdb","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Actually I might try the separate .inc approach. I like the idea of keeping the whole multithreaded collision pipeline within one file. It's an easy way to get a vertical slice of the BVH, while the other inc's are broken up horizontally by layer.\r\n\r\nI will play with a few different ways and see what feels neat.","created_at":"2026-08-25T10:57:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:57:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3852270781","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3852270781"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122686#discussion_r3852270781"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122686"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3852270781/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":46,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3843318955,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}]